## Anatomy of the four-legged families drawn by QuadrupedModel, in metres at
## the family's base size, facing -Z, right side +X (legs are mirrored):
##   bones   centre-line bone rest positions: hips, spine, chest, neck, neck2, head
##   torso   rows [z, centre y, half width, half height] from the tail root to
##           the back of the skull (one smooth tube through all of them)
##   front / hind  joint chain of the right legs: [blade or pelvis top (inside
##           the body), shoulder / hip, elbow / stifle, wrist / hock, foot]
##   front_prof / hind_prof  limb radii [t, half width, half depth, offset back]
##   tail    joint chain (first = root) and radii per joint
##   foot    "paw" | "bear" | "hoof" | "hare" | "webbed"
##   gait    cycle length (m per stride at a walk), lift (m), duty factors
## Muscles are shaped by the radii: a wolf's deep chest and tucked loin, a
## bear's shoulder hump, a deer's slender cannons and long neck.

